[38;2;124;124;124mWe claim the minimum size of a set of points in PG(d,q) intersecting every line [0m[38;2;124;124;124mis (q^d - 1)/(q-1), the number of points in a hyperplane.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Upper bound:** A hyperplane H in PG(d,q) is a (d-1)-dimensional projective [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msubspace containing (q^d - 1)/(q-1) points. Every line ℓ in PG(d,q) meets H: [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mviewing PG(d,q) as the lattice of subspaces of GF(q)^{d+1}, a line corresponds [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mto a 2-dimensional subspace and H to a d-dimensional subspace. By dimension [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcounting, dim(ℓ ∩ H) ≥ 2 + d - (d+1) = 1, so they share at least a point. Thus H[0m[38;2;124;124;124mis a blocking set of size (q^d - 1)/(q-1).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Lower bound:** We proceed by induction on d.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m*Base case d = 1:* PG(1,q) is a single line with q+1 points. Any single point [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mintersects this line, so the minimum is 1 = (q^1 - 1)/(q-1). ✓[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m*Base case d = 2:* PG(2,q) is a projective plane. Let S be a blocking set. If S [0m[38;2;124;124;124mcontains all q² + q + 1 points, then |S| ≥ q+1 trivially. Otherwise, there [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mexists a point P ∉ S. The q+1 lines through P are pairwise distinct and meet [0m
[38;2;124;124;124monly at P. Each must contain a point of S (other than P, since P ∉ S), and these[0m[38;2;124;124;124mpoints are distinct (since two lines through P share only P). Thus |S| ≥ q+1 = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(q²-1)/(q-1). ✓[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m*Inductive step (d ≥ 3):* Assume the result for PG(d-1,q). Let S be a blocking [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mset in PG(d,q). For any hyperplane H ≅ PG(d-1,q), the set S ∩ H is a blocking [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mset in H: every line contained in H must be met by S, and the meeting point lies[0m[38;2;124;124;124min H, hence in S ∩ H. By the induction hypothesis, |S ∩ H| ≥ (q^{d-1} - 1)/[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(q-1).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mCount pairs (P, H) where P ∈ S and H is a hyperplane containing P. Each point [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mlies in (q^d - 1)/(q-1) hyperplanes (the hyperplanes through a point correspond [0m[38;2;124;124;124mto hyperplanes of the quotient PG(d-1,q)). The total number of hyperplanes is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(q^{d+1} - 1)/(q-1). Thus:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m|S| · (q^d - 1)/(q-1) = Σ_H |S ∩ H| ≥ (q^{d+1} - 1)/(q-1) · (q^{d-1} - 1)/(q-1)[0m

